ress><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUKUSHIMA, MASAKAZU</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, NORIHIKO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAIHO PHARMACEUTICAL CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO, NORIYUKI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>FUKUSHIMA MASAKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI NORIHIKO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO NORIYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUKUSHIMA, MASAKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, NORIHIKO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMAMOTO, NORIYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Agents for relieving the side effects of antitumor agents which contain as the active ingredient 5-chloro-6-(2-iminopyrrolidin-1-yl)methyl-2,4(1H,3H)-pyrimidinedione represented by formula (1) or pharmaceutically acceptable salts thereof.  5-Chloro-6-(2-iminopyrrolidin-1-yl)methyl-2,4(1H,3H)-pyrimidinedione (1) and its salts have an advantage that they have an activity of inhibiting inflammation in the digestive tract induced by the administration of antitumor agents and thus can relieve diarrhea or body weight loss in association with the administration of chemotherapeutics for cancer without worsening the antitumor effect.  Owing to these characteristics, they are highly useful in relieving the side effects, thereby enabling continuous chemotherapy for cancer and preventing physical exhaustion.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Cette invention concerne des agents atténuant les effets secondaires d'agents antitumoraux. Le principe actif de ces agents atténuateurs est 5-chloro-6-(2-imminopyrrolidine-1-yl)méthyl-2, 4(1H, 3H)-pyriminedione représenté par la formule (1) ou des sels de ce composé acceptables au plan pharmaceutique. Le 5-chloro-6-(2-imminopyrrolidine-1-yl)méthyl-2, 4(1H, 3H)-pyriminedione (1) et ses sels offrent l'avantage d'inhiber l'inflammation de l'appareil digestif provoquée par l'administration d'agents antitumoraux et donc d'atténuer la diarrhées ou la perte de poids associée associée à la chimiothérapie du cancer sans réduire l'effet antitumoral. Au vu de ces caractéristiques, ces agents conviennent particulièrement bien pour atténuer les effets secondaires, ce qui permet de ne pas interrompre la chimiothérapie et d'empêcher l'épuisement physique du malade.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>